# Gate step 1449-4qqu — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. install-windows.ps1's --reset-state probe. It runs the flag
# with the opt-out set; a supporting tray announces the skip and re-inits the
# EXISTING state. When that state is broken the re-init fails, and the probe
# used to read that exit code as "this tray predates --reset-state", skipping
# the one repair the guest needed (measured on yolanda 2026-09-27, v56.9.27.2).
# The probe now also reads the skip line (tillandsias-core's pinned phrase).
#
# The fixture cuts the probe between exact-once markers and RUNS it in
# PowerShell against four stub trays (.cmd): unknown flag, accepted-but-failed,
# accepted-ok, unclaimed failure. Pre-fix: the accepted-but-failed arm FAILS.
# Without PowerShell and cmd.exe (a Linux gate) it skips by name.
#
# STEP_SCRIPT is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the installer's --reset-state probe tells a failed re-init from an old tray (1449-4qqu)"
STEP_SCRIPT="scripts/test-installer-reset-probe.sh"
STEP_ERROR="the installer's --reset-state probe again reads a failed re-init as an old tray and would skip the repair (1449-4qqu); see which arm failed above"
STEP_OK="installer reset probe distinguishes unsupported from ran-and-failed"
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="yolanda 2026-09-28 msys ok:reset-probe-fixture:4"
